rst_condition\n\n# Second condition: x of Nate's dogs are reassigned to Denali\ndenali_dogs_second_condition = denali_dogs_initial + x\nnate_dogs_second_condition = nate_dogs_initial - x\nratio_second_condition = denali_dogs_second_condition / nate_dogs_second_condition\n\n# Check if the ratios are equal\nprint((ratio_first_condition, ratio_second_condition))\n```", "To solve the problem, we need to set up the equations based on the given conditions and solve for \\( x \\).\n\n1. **Initial Setup:**\n   - Denali is responsible for 16 dogs.\n   - Nate is responsible for 12 dogs.\n   - The ratio of Denali's pay to Nate's pay is \\(\\frac{16k}{12k} = \\frac{4}{3}\\), where \\( k \\) is the pay per dog.\n\n2. **First Condition:**\n   - If Denali starts walking \\( 4x \\) more dogs, she will be responsible for \\( 16 + 4x \\) dogs.\n   - Nate stays at 12 dogs.\n   - The ratio of Denali's pay to Nate's pay remains the same, so \\(\\frac{(16 + 4x)k}{12k} = \\frac{4}{3}\\).\n\n3. **Second Condition:**\n   - If \\( x \\) of Nate's dogs are reassigned to Denali, Denali will be responsible for \\( 16 + x \\) dogs and Nate will be responsible for \\( 12 - x \\) dogs.\n   - The ratio of Denali's pay to Nate's pay remains the same, so \\(\\frac{(16 + x)k}{(12 - x)k} = \\frac{4}{3}\\).\n\n4. **Solve the Equations:**\n   - From the first condition: \\(\\frac{16 + 4x}{12} = \\frac{4}{3}\\).\n   - From the second condition: \\(\\frac{16 + x}{12 - x} = \\frac{4}{3}\\).\n\nLet's solve these equations step-by-step using Python and sympy.\n\n```python\nimport sympy as sp\n\n# Define the variable\nx = sp.symbols('x')\n\n# First condition equation\neq1 = sp.Eq((16 + 4*x) / 12, 4 / 3)\n\n# Second condition equation\neq2 = sp.Eq((16 + x) / (12 - x), 4 / 3)\n\n# Solve the equations\nsolution1 = sp.solve(eq1, x)\nsolution2 = sp.solve(eq2, x)\n\n# Find the common solution\ncommon_solution = set(solution1).intersection(set(solution2))\nprint(common_solution)\n```\n```output\nset()\n```\nIt seems 