lex number\nz = 7 + 2j\n\n# Perform a 90 degree counter-clockwise rotation by multiplying by i\nz_rotated = z * 1j\n\n# Output the resulting complex number\nprint(z_rotated)\n```\n```output\n(-2+7j)\n```\nThe resulting complex number after a $90^\\circ$ counter-clockwise rotation of $7 + 2i$ is $\\boxed{-2 + 7i}$.", "When we rotate a complex number $z = a + bi$ by $90^\\circ$ counterclockwise around the origin, it is equivalent to multiplying $z$ by $i$. This is because $i$ represents a $90^\\circ$ rotation in the complex plane. So, if $z = 7 + 2i$, then the resulting complex number after a $90^\\circ$ rotation is $i(7 + 2i)$. Let's calculate this step-by-step.\n\n1. Distribute the $i$:\n\\[ i(7 + 2i) = 7i + 2i^2. \\]\n2. Since $i^2 = -1$, we can substitute $-1$ for $i^2$:\n\\[ 7i + 2(-1) = 7i - 2. \\]\n3. Rearrange the terms to get the final complex number:\n\\[ -2 + 7i. \\]\n\nSo, the resulting complex number is $-2 + 7i$. Let's confirm this with Python code.\n```python\n# Define the complex number\nz = 7 + 2j\n\n# Rotate the complex number by 90 degrees counterclockwise (multiply by i)\nrotated_z = z * 1j\n\n# Output the resulting complex number\nprint(rotated_z)\n```\n```output\n(-2+7j)\n```\nThe resulting complex number after a $90^\\circ$ rotation around the origin is $\\boxed{-2 + 7i}$.", "To find the result of a $90^\\circ$ rotation around the origin in the counter-clockwise direction applied to the complex number $7 + 2i$, we can use the property of complex numbers. A $90^\\circ$ counter-clockwise rotation of a complex number $z = a + bi$ around the origin is equivalent to multiplying $z$ by $i$. This is because $i$ represents a $90^\\circ$ counter-clockwise rotation in the complex plane.\n\nSo, if we have the complex number $z = 7 + 2i$, the result of the $90^\\circ$ rotation is given by:\n\\[ z' = i \\cdot (7 + 2i) \\]\n\nLet's perform the multiplication:\n\\[ z' = i \\cdot 7 + i \\cdot 2i = 7i + 2i^2 \\]\nSince $i^2 = -1$, we get:\n\\[ z' = 7i + 2(-1) = 