 is 7. Dividing 121 by 7 gives:\n  \\[\n  121 \\div 7 \\approx 17.2857\n  \\]\n  which is not an integer, so 121 is not divisible by 7. We check the next prime number, which is 11. Dividing 121 by 11 gives:\n  \\[\n  121 \\div 11 = 11\n  \\]\n  So, we have:\n  \\[\n  121 = 11 \\times 11\n  \\]\n  Therefore, the prime factorization of 242 is:\n  \\[\n  242 = 2 \\times 11 \\times 11\n  \\]\n\nStep 2: Simplify the square root by taking out pairs of prime factors.\n- We have one pair of 11s and one 2 left over. We can take the pair of 11s out of the square root:\n  \\[\n  \\sqrt{242} = \\sqrt{2 \\times 11 \\times 11} = \\sqrt{2} \\times \\sqrt{11 \\times 11} = \\sqrt{2} \\times 11 = 11\\sqrt{2}\n  \\]\n\nTherefore, the simplified form of \\(\\sqrt{242}\\) is \\(\\boxed{11\\sqrt{2}}\\).\n\nFind the least squares solution to the linear system given by the matrix\n$\\left(\n\\begin{array}{ccc}\n-1 & 1 & 3 \\\\\n-1 & 1 & 1 \\\\\n2 & -3 & 1 \\\\\n-2 & 1 & -3 \\\\\n\\end{array}\n\\right)$ and the vector\n$\\left(\n\\begin{array}{c}\n-1.08 \\\\\n-2.29 \\\\\n0.2 \\\\\n-1.7 \\\\\n\\end{array}\n\\right)$. To find the least squares solution to the linear system given by the matrix \\( A \\) and the vector \\( b \\), we need to solve the normal equations \\( A^T A x = A^T b \\).\n\nFirst, let's compute \\( A^T \\):\n\\[\nA^T = \\left(\n\\begin{array}{cccc}\n-1 & -1 & 2 & -2 \\\\\n1 & 1 & -3 & 1 \\\\\n3 & 1 & 1 & -3 \\\\\n\\end{array}\n\\right)\n\\]\n\nNext, we compute \\( A^T A \\):\n\\[\nA^T A = \\left(\n\\begin{array}{ccc}\n(-1)(-1) + (-1)(-1) + 2(2) + (-2)(-2) & (-1)(1) + (-1)(1) + 2(-3) + (-2)(1) & (-1)(3) + (-1)(1) + 2(1) + (-2)(-3) \\\\\n(1)(-1) + (1)(-1) + (-3)(2) + (1)(-2) & (1)(1) + (1)(1) + (-3)(-3) + (1)(1) & (1)(3) + (1)(1) + (-3)(1) + (1)(-3) \\\\\n(3)(-1) + (1)(-1) + (1)(2) + (-3)(-2) & (3)(1) + (1)(1) + (1)(-3) + (-3)(1) & (3)(3) + (1)(1) + (1)(1) + (-3)(-3) \\\\\n\\end{array}\n\\right)\n\\]\n\\[\nA^T A = \\left(\n\\begin{array}{ccc}\n1 + 1 + 4 + 4 & -1 - 1 - 6 - 2 &