cy.\n```python\n# Define the inequalities\r\nfrom sympy import symbols, solve, And\r\n\r\n# Define the variable\r\nx = symbols('x')\r\n\r\n# Define the inequalities\r\ninequality1 = -4 < 2 * (x - 1)\r\ninequality2 = 2 * (x - 1) < 8\r\n\r\n# Solve the inequalities\r\nsolution1 = solve(inequality1, x)\r\nsolution2 = solve(inequality2, x)\r\n\r\n# Find the intersection of the solutions\r\nsolution = And(solution1, solution2)\r\n\r\n# Extract the bounds\r\na = solution.lhs\r\nb = solution.rhs\r\n\r\n# Calculate a + b\r\nresult = a + b\r\nprint(result)\n```\n```output\nAttributeError: 'And' object has no attribute 'lhs'\n```\nIt seems there was an issue with how the solution was extracted from the `And` object. Let's correct this by solving the inequalities separately and then combining the results manually.\n\nWe'll solve the inequalities step-by-step and then find the intersection of the solutions.\n```python\n# Solve the inequalities separately\r\nsolution1 = solve(inequality1, x)\r\nsolution2 = solve(inequality2, x)\r\n\r\n# Extract the bounds manually\r\na = solution1[0].rhs\r\nb = solution2[0].lhs\r\n\r\n# Calculate a + b\r\nresult = a + b\r\nprint(result)\n```\n```output\nNameError: name 'solve' is not defined\n```\nIt seems there was an issue with the previous approach. Let's solve the inequalities step-by-step manually and then find the intersection of the solutions.\n\n1. Solve \\(-4 < 2(x - 1)\\):\n\\[\n-4 < 2(x - 1) \\implies -2 < x - 1 \\implies -1 < x\n\\]\nSo, we have \\(x > -1\\).\n\n2. Solve \\(2(x - 1) < 8\\):\n\\[\n2(x - 1) < 8 \\implies x - 1 < 4 \\implies x < 5\n\\]\nSo, we have \\(x < 5\\).\n\nCombining these two results, we get:\n\\[\n-1 < x < 5\n\\]\nThis is in the form \\(a < x < b\\), where \\(a = -1\\) and \\(b = 5\\).\n\nNow, we need to find the value of \\(a + b\\):\n\\[\na + b = -1 + 5 = 4\n\\]\n\nLet's verify this with a simpler Python code snippet to ensure accuracy.\n```python\n# Define the bounds manually\r\na = -1\r\nb = 5\r\n\r\n# Calc