ngle EAD + \\angle ADE = 35^\\circ + 35^\\circ = 70^\\circ \\).\n\nSo, the measure of angle \\( \\angle AFD \\) is \\( 70^\\circ \\).\n\nLet's confirm this with Python and sympy:\n\n```python\nimport sympy as sp\n\n# Define the variable\nx = sp.symbols('x')\n\n# Set up the equation based on the sum of angles in the quadrilateral\nequation = 6*x + 70 + 80 - 360\n\n# Solve for x\nsolution = sp.solve(equation, x)[0]\n\n# Calculate the measure of angle AFD\nangle_AFD = 2 * solution\n\nprint(angle_AFD)\n```\n```output\n70\n```\nThe measure of angle \\( \\angle AFD \\) is \\(\\boxed{70^\\circ}\\).", "To find the degree measure of angle \\( \\angle AFD \\) in the given quadrilateral \\(ABCD\\), we need to analyze the trisected angles and use the properties of the quadrilateral and the angles formed.\n\nGiven:\n- \\( \\angle BAD \\) and \\( \\angle CDA \\) are trisected.\n- The trisected angles are labeled as \\(x\\), \\(x\\), and \\(x\\) for \\( \\angle BAD \\) and \\(y\\), \\(y\\), and \\(y\\) for \\( \\angle CDA \\).\n- The angles at \\(A\\) and \\(D\\) are given as \\(110^\\circ\\) and \\(100^\\circ\\) respectively.\n\nFirst, let's determine the values of \\(x\\) and \\(y\\):\n- Since \\( \\angle BAD = 3x \\) and \\( \\angle BAD = 110^\\circ \\), we have \\( 3x = 110^\\circ \\). So, \\( x = \\frac{110^\\circ}{3} \\).\n- Since \\( \\angle CDA = 3y \\) and \\( \\angle CDA = 100^\\circ \\), we have \\( 3y = 100^\\circ \\). So, \\( y = \\frac{100^\\circ}{3} \\).\n\nNext, we need to find the measure of \\( \\angle AFD \\). To do this, we will use the fact that the sum of the angles around point \\(F\\) is \\(360^\\circ\\).\n\nThe angles around point \\(F\\) are:\n- \\( \\angle AFD \\)\n- \\( \\angle AFE \\) (which is composed of two trisected angles from \\( \\angle BAD \\))\n- \\( \\angle EFD \\) (which is composed of two trisected angles from \\( \\angle CDA \\))\n\nSo, \\( \\angle AFD + \\angle AFE + \\angle EFD = 360^\\circ \\).\n\nSince \\( \\angle AFE = 2x \\) and \\( 