efore (with some tolerance)\n    if np.isclose(equation(root), 0, atol=1e-6):\n        roots.append(root)\n\n# Remove duplicates by converting to a set and then back to a list\nunique_roots = list(set(np.round(roots, decimals=6)))\n\nprint(unique_roots)\n```\n```output\n[0.0, 11.000000000000002]\n```\nThe real roots of the equation are \\(0\\) and \\(11\\). Therefore, the final answer is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{0, 11}\n\\]", "To solve the given equation, we need to find the values of \\(x\\) that satisfy:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{(x + 1)(x - 3)}{5(x + 2)(x - 4)} + \\frac{(x + 3)(x - 5)}{9(x + 4)(x - 6)} - \\frac{2(x + 5)(x - 7)}{13(x + 6)(x - 8)} = \\frac{92}{585}.\n\\]\n\nFirst, let's simplify the left-hand side of the equation. We'll define the left-hand side as a function and then solve for the roots. We'll use Python's `sympy` library to handle the algebraic manipulations and find the roots.\n\nHere's the step-by-step code to solve the equation:\n\n1. Define the variable and the equation.\n2. Simplify the left-hand side of the equation.\n3. Solve the equation for \\(x\\).\n\nLet's implement this in Python:\n\n```python\nimport sympy as sp\n\n# Define the variable\nx = sp.symbols('x')\n\n# Define the left-hand side of the equation\nlhs = ( (x + 1)*(x - 3) / (5*(x + 2)*(x - 4)) +\n        (x + 3)*(x - 5) / (9*(x + 4)*(x - 6)) -\n        2*(x + 5)*(x - 7) / (13*(x + 6)*(x - 8)) )\n\n# Define the right-hand side of the equation\nrhs = 92 / 585\n\n# Create the equation\nequation = sp.Eq(lhs, rhs)\n\n# Solve the equation for x\nsolutions = sp.solve(equation, x)\n\n# Filter out any non-real solutions\nreal_solutions = [sol.evalf() for sol in solutions if sol.is_real]\n\n# Print the real solutions\nprint(real_solutions)\n```\n```output\n[-7.00000000000000, -0.506492250872309, 2.00000000000000, 17.5064922508723]\n```\nThe real roots of the equation\n\n\\[\n\\frac{(x + 1)(x - 3)}{5(x + 2)(x - 4)} + \\frac{(x + 3)(x - 5)}{9(x + 4)(x - 6)} - \\frac{2(x + 5)(x - 7)}{13(x + 6)(x - 8)} = \\fra