need to compute the distances from these points to the point \\((-3, 2)\\). The distance formula between two points \\((x_1, y_1)\\) and \\((x_2, y_2)\\) is:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Distance} = \\sqrt{(x_2 - x_1)^2 + (y_2 - y_1)^2}\n\\]\n\nFor each point, the distance to \\((-3, 2)\\) is:\n\n1. For \\((-3 + \\sqrt{36 + 4\\sqrt{41}}, 10 + \\sqrt{41})\\):\n\\[\n\\text{Distance} = \\sqrt{(\\sqrt{36 + 4\\sqrt{41}})^2 + (10 + \\sqrt{41} - 2)^2} = \\sqrt{36 + 4\\sqrt{41} + (8 + \\sqrt{41})^2} = \\sqrt{36 + 4\\sqrt{41} + 64 + 16\\sqrt{41} + 41} = \\sqrt{141 + 20\\sqrt{41}}\n\\]\n\n2. For \\((-3 - \\sqrt{36 + 4\\sqrt{41}}, 10 + \\sqrt{41})\\):\n\\[\n\\text{Distance} = \\sqrt{(-\\sqrt{36 + 4\\sqrt{41}})^2 + (10 + \\sqrt{41} - 2)^2} = \\sqrt{36 + 4\\sqrt{41} + (8 + \\sqrt{41})^2} = \\sqrt{36 + 4\\sqrt{41} + 64 + 16\\sqrt{41} + 41} = \\sqrt{141 + 20\\sqrt{41}}\n\\]\n\n3. For \\((-3 + \\sqrt{36 - 4\\sqrt{41}}, 10 - \\sqrt{41})\\):\n\\[\n\\text{Distance} = \\sqrt{(\\sqrt{36 - 4\\sqrt{41}})^2 + (10 - \\sqrt{41} - 2)^2} = \\sqrt{36 - 4\\sqrt{41} + (8 - \\sqrt{41})^2} = \\sqrt{36 - 4\\sqrt{41} + 64 - 16\\sqrt{41} + 41} = \\sqrt{141 - 20\\sqrt{41}}\n\\]\n\n4. For \\((-3 - \\sqrt{36 - 4\\sqrt{41}}, 10 - \\sqrt{41})\\):\n\\[\n\\text{Distance} = \\sqrt{(-\\sqrt{36 - 4\\sqrt{41}})^2 + (10 - \\sqrt{41} - 2)^2} = \\sqrt{36 - 4\\sqrt{41} + (8 - \\sqrt{41})^2} = \\sqrt{36 - 4\\sqrt{41} + 64 - 16\\sqrt{41} + 41} = \\sqrt{141 - 20\\sqrt{41}}\n\\]\n\nThe sum of the distances is:\n\\[\n\\sqrt{141 + 20\\sqrt{41}} + \\sqrt{141 + 20\\sqrt{41}} + \\sqrt{141 - 20\\sqrt{41}} + \\sqrt{141 - 20\\sqrt{41}} = 2\\sqrt{141 + 20\\sqrt{41}} + 2\\sqrt{141 - 20\\sqrt{41}}\n\\]\n\nLet's compute this sum using Python to ensure accuracy.\n```python\nimport math\r\n\r\n# Define the distances\r\ndistance1 = math.sqrt(141 + 20 * math.sqrt(41))\r\ndistance2 = math.sqrt(141 - 20 * math.sqrt(41))\r\n\r\n# Sum of the distances\r\ntotal_distance = 2 * (distance1 + distance2)\r\nprint(total_distance)\n```\n```output\n41.9999999999