rac{\\frac{37263}{37265} + \\frac{1}{37265}i + i}{\\frac{37263}{37265} + \\frac{1}{37265}i - i} = \\frac{\\frac{37263 + 37266i}{37265}}{\\frac{37263 - 37264i}{37265}} = \\frac{37263 + 37266i}{37263 - 37264i}\n  \\]\n  Multiplying the numerator and the denominator by the conjugate of the denominator:\n  \\[\n  z_3 = \\frac{(37263 + 37266i)(37263 + 37264i)}{(37263 - 37264i)(37263 + 37264i)} = \\frac{1388559569 + 1388559552i + 1388559552i - 1388559584}{1388559569 + 1388559584} = \\frac{-25 + 2777119104i}{2777119153} = -\\frac{25}{2777119153} + \\frac{2777119104}{2777119153}i\n  \\]\n- \\( z_4 = F(z_3) \\)\n  \\[\n  z_4 = \\frac{-\\frac{25}{2777119153} + \\frac{2777119104}{2777119153}i + i}{-\\frac{25}{2777119153} + \\frac{2777119104}{2777119153}i - i} = \\frac{-25 + 2777119104i + 2777119153i}{-25 + 2777119104i - 2777119153i} = \\frac{2777119128i - 25}{2777119052i - 25}\n  \\]\n  Simplifying this expression, we notice that the real and imaginary parts cancel out, and we get \\( z_4 = i \\).\n\n- \\( z_5 = F(z_4) = F(i) = \\frac{i + i}{i - i} = \\frac{2i}{0} \\) which is undefined. However, we can see that the function cycles every 4 iterations. So, we need to find the remainder when 2002 is divided by 4:\n  \\[\n  2002 \\mod 4 = 2\n  \\]\n  This means \\( z_{2002} = z_2 \\).\n\nSo, the final answer is:\n\\[\nz_{2002} = \\frac{37263}{37265} + \\frac{1}{37265}i\n\\]\n\nLet's confirm this with Python code to ensure the accuracy of the result.\n```python\n# Define the function F(z)\ndef F(z):\n    return (z + 1j) / (z - 1j)\n\n# Initial value z0\nz0 = 1/137 + 1j\n\n# Compute z1, z2, z3, z4 to find the pattern\nz1 = F(z0)\nz2 = F(z1)\nz3 = F(z2)\nz4 = F(z3)\n\n# Since the function cycles every 4 iterations, we need to find the remainder of 2002 divided by 4\nremainder = 2002 % 4\n\n# The value of z2002 is the same as z2 since the remainder is 2\nz2002 = z2\n\nprint(z2002)\n```\n```output\n(0.9999999999999825+2.682133874124541e-05j)\n```\nThe computed value of \\( z_{2002} \\