\\frac{37413 + 37266i}{37413 - 37264i} \\cdot \\frac{37413 + 37264i}{37413 + 37264i} = \\frac{(37413 + 37266i)(37413 + 37264i)}{37413^2 + 37264^2} = \\frac{37413^2 + 37413 \\cdot 37264i + 37266 \\cdot 37413i - 37266 \\cdot 37264}{37413^2 + 37264^2} = \\frac{37413^2 - 37266 \\cdot 37264 + (37413 \\cdot 37264 + 37266 \\cdot 37413)i}{37413^2 + 37264^2} = \\frac{137}{137} + i = 1 + i \\)\n5. \\( z_4 = F(z_3) = F(1 + i) = \\frac{1 + i + i}{1 + i - i} = \\frac{1 + 2i}{1} = 1 + 2i \\)\n6. \\( z_5 = F(z_4) = F(1 + 2i) = \\frac{1 + 2i + i}{1 + 2i - i} = \\frac{1 + 3i}{1 + i} \\cdot \\frac{1 - i}{1 - i} = \\frac{(1 + 3i)(1 - i)}{1 + 1} = \\frac{1 - i + 3i + 3}{2} = \\frac{4 + 2i}{2} = 2 + i \\)\n7. \\( z_6 = F(z_5) = F(2 + i) = \\frac{2 + i + i}{2 + i - i} = \\frac{2 + 2i}{2} = 1 + i \\)\n\nFrom the above calculations, we can see that \\( z_3 = 1 + i \\), \\( z_4 = 1 + 2i \\), and \\( z_5 = 2 + i \\). After this, the sequence repeats every 4 iterations. Therefore, \\( z_{2002} = z_2 \\).\n\nSince \\( z_2 = -137 \\), the final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{-137}\n\\]", "To solve the problem, we need to analyze the function \\( F(z) = \\frac{z + i}{z - i} \\) and its iterations. Let's start by computing the first few iterations of \\( F \\) to see if we can find a pattern.\n\nGiven \\( z_0 = \\frac{1}{137} + i \\), we can compute \\( z_1 = F(z_0) \\), \\( z_2 = F(z_1) \\), and so on, to see if there is a repeating cycle.\n\nFirst, let's compute \\( z_1 \\):\n\\[ z_1 = F(z_0) = \\frac{\\frac{1}{137} + i + i}{\\frac{1}{137} + i - i} = \\frac{\\frac{1}{137} + 2i}{\\frac{1}{137}} = 1 + 274i. \\]\n\nNext, let's compute \\( z_2 \\):\n\\[ z_2 = F(z_1) = \\frac{1 + 274i + i}{1 + 274i - i} = \\frac{1 + 275i}{1 + 273i}. \\]\nTo simplify this, we multiply the numerator and the denominator by the conjugate of the denominator:\n\\[ z_2 = \\frac{(1 + 275i)(1 - 273i)}{(1 + 273i)(1 - 273i)} = \\frac{1 - 273i + 275i + 74775}{1 + 74529} = \\frac{74776 + 2i}{74530} = \\frac{37388}{37265} + \\frac{1}{3