nd{pmatrix}, \\quad \\overrightarrow{OB} = \\begin{pmatrix} -3 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1 \\end{pmatrix}\n\\]\n\nThe cross product $\\overrightarrow{OA} \\times \\overrightarrow{OB}$ is calculated as follows:\n\\[\n\\overrightarrow{OA} \\times \\overrightarrow{OB} = \\begin{vmatrix}\n\\mathbf{i} & \\mathbf{j} & \\mathbf{k} \\\\\n1 & 2 & 3 \\\\\n-3 & -2 & 1\n\\end{vmatrix}\n= \\mathbf{i}(2 \\cdot 1 - 3 \\cdot (-2)) - \\mathbf{j}(1 \\cdot 1 - 3 \\cdot (-3)) + \\mathbf{k}(1 \\cdot (-2) - 2 \\cdot (-3))\n= \\mathbf{i}(2 + 6) - \\mathbf{j}(1 + 9) + \\mathbf{k}(-2 + 6)\n= 8\\mathbf{i} - 10\\mathbf{j} + 4\\mathbf{k}\n\\]\n\nSo, the cross product is:\n\\[\n\\overrightarrow{OA} \\times \\overrightarrow{OB} = \\begin{pmatrix} 8 \\\\ -10 \\\\ 4 \\end{pmatrix}\n\\]\n\nThe magnitude of this vector is:\n\\[\n\\|\\overrightarrow{OA} \\times \\overrightarrow{OB}\\| = \\sqrt{8^2 + (-10)^2 + 4^2} = \\sqrt{64 + 100 + 16} = \\sqrt{180} = 6\\sqrt{5}\n\\]\n\nThe area of the parallelogram formed by $\\overrightarrow{OA}$ and $\\overrightarrow{OB}$ is $6\\sqrt{5}$. Therefore, the area of triangle $OAB$ is half of this value:\n\\[\n\\text{Area of triangle } OAB = \\frac{1}{2} \\times 6\\sqrt{5} = 3\\sqrt{5}\n\\]\n\nLet's confirm this with Python code.\n```python\nimport numpy as np\n\n# Define the vectors OA and OB\nOA = np.array([1, 2, 3])\nOB = np.array([-3, -2, 1])\n\n# Calculate the cross product of OA and OB\ncross_product = np.cross(OA, OB)\n\n# Calculate the magnitude of the cross product\nmagnitude = np.linalg.norm(cross_product)\n\n# The area of the triangle is half the magnitude of the cross product\narea_triangle = 0.5 * magnitude\nprint(area_triangle)\n```\n```output\n6.708203932499369\n```\nThe area of triangle $OAB$ is $3\\sqrt{5}$, which is approximately $6.708$. Therefore, the final answer is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{3\\sqrt{5}}\n\\]", "To find the area of triangle \\(OAB\\), we can use the cross product of vectors \\(\\overrightarrow{OA}\\) and \\(\\overrightarrow{OB}\\). The magnitude of the 