agnitude of the cross product\narea_triangle = magnitude / 2\n\nprint(area_triangle)\n```\n```output\n4.08248290463863\n```\nThe area of triangle \\(OAB\\) is \\(\\boxed{4.08248290463863}\\).", "To find the area of the triangle \\(OAB\\), we can use the cross product of vectors \\(\\overrightarrow{OA}\\) and \\(\\overrightarrow{OB}\\). The magnitude of the cross product of two vectors gives the area of the parallelogram formed by these vectors. The area of the triangle is half of this value.\n\nThe cross product of vectors \\(\\overrightarrow{OA} = \\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 3 \\end{pmatrix}\\) and \\(\\overrightarrow{OB} = \\begin{pmatrix} -3 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1 \\end{pmatrix}\\) is given by:\n\n\\[\n\\overrightarrow{OA} \\times \\overrightarrow{OB} = \\begin{vmatrix}\n\\mathbf{i} & \\mathbf{j} & \\mathbf{k} \\\\\n1 & 2 & 3 \\\\\n-3 & -2 & 1\n\\end{vmatrix}\n= \\mathbf{i}(2 \\cdot 1 - 3 \\cdot (-2)) - \\mathbf{j}(1 \\cdot 1 - 3 \\cdot (-3)) + \\mathbf{k}(1 \\cdot (-2) - 2 \\cdot (-3))\n= \\mathbf{i}(2 + 6) - \\mathbf{j}(1 + 9) + \\mathbf{k}(-2 + 6)\n= \\begin{pmatrix} 8 \\\\ -10 \\\\ 4 \\end{pmatrix}\n\\]\n\nThe magnitude of the cross product vector is:\n\n\\[\n\\|\\overrightarrow{OA} \\times \\overrightarrow{OB}\\| = \\sqrt{8^2 + (-10)^2 + 4^2} = \\sqrt{64 + 100 + 16} = \\sqrt{180} = 6\\sqrt{5}\n\\]\n\nThe area of triangle \\(OAB\\) is half of this value:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Area} = \\frac{1}{2} \\times 6\\sqrt{5} = 3\\sqrt{5}\n\\]\n\nLet's confirm this with Python code.\n```python\nimport numpy as np\r\n\r\n# Define the vectors OA and OB\r\nOA = np.array([1, 2, 3])\r\nOB = np.array([-3, -2, 1])\r\n\r\n# Compute the cross product of OA and OB\r\ncross_product = np.cross(OA, OB)\r\n\r\n# Compute the magnitude of the cross product\r\nmagnitude = np.linalg.norm(cross_product)\r\n\r\n# The area of the triangle is half the magnitude of the cross product\r\narea_triangle = 0.5 * magnitude\r\nprint(area_triangle)\n```\n```output\n6.708203932499369\n```\nThe computed area of th