 100 \\div 7 \\approx 14.2857 \\)\n   - The smallest integer greater than 14.2857 is 15.\n   - Multiply 15 by 7: \\( 15 \\times 7 = 105 \\)\n   - So, the first multiple of 7 in this range is 105.\n\n2. **Identify the last multiple of 7 less than or equal to 200:**\n   - Divide 200 by 7: \\( 200 \\div 7 \\approx 28.5714 \\)\n   - The largest integer less than 28.5714 is 28.\n   - Multiply 28 by 7: \\( 28 \\times 7 = 196 \\)\n   - So, the last multiple of 7 in this range is 196.\n\n3. **Determine the number of multiples of 7 between 105 and 196:**\n   - The sequence of multiples of 7 is an arithmetic sequence where the first term \\( a = 105 \\) and the common difference \\( d = 7 \\).\n   - The \\( n \\)-th term of an arithmetic sequence is given by \\( a_n = a + (n-1)d \\).\n   - Set \\( a_n = 196 \\) and solve for \\( n \\):\n     \\[\n     196 = 105 + (n-1) \\times 7\n     \\]\n     \\[\n     196 = 105 + 7n - 7\n     \\]\n     \\[\n     196 = 98 + 7n\n     \\]\n     \\[\n     98 = 7n\n     \\]\n     \\[\n     n = \\frac{98}{7} = 14\n     \\]\n   - There are 14 multiples of 7 between 105 and 196.\n\n4. **Calculate the sum of these multiples:**\n   - The sum \\( S_n \\) of the first \\( n \\) terms of an arithmetic sequence is given by:\n     \\[\n     S_n = \\frac{n}{2} \\times (a + l)\n     \\]\n     where \\( l \\) is the last term.\n   - Here, \\( n = 14 \\), \\( a = 105 \\), and \\( l = 196 \\):\n     \\[\n     S_{14} = \\frac{14}{2} \\times (105 + 196)\n     \\]\n     \\[\n     S_{14} = 7 \\times 301\n     \\]\n     \\[\n     S_{14} = 2107\n     \\]\n\nTherefore, the sum of all multiples of 7 between 100 and 200 is \\(\\boxed{2107}\\).\n\nWhat is the purpose of the "100 Horizontal Mixed Operations Questions (Facts 1 to 5) Euro Format (J)" math worksheet? The "100 Horizontal Mixed Operations Questions (Facts 1 to 5) Euro Format (J)" math worksheet is designed to provide practice in mixed operations, including addition, subtraction, multiplication, and division,