luate P(-2)\nremainder = P(-2)\nprint(remainder)\n```\n```output\n12\n```\nThe remainder when \\((5x + 9)^{611} + (x + 5)^{11} + (x - 1)^{11} + 3x^2 + 1\\) is divided by \\(x + 2\\) is \\(\\boxed{12}\\).", "To find the remainder when the polynomial \\(P(x) = (5x + 9)^{611} + (x + 5)^{11} + (x - 1)^{11} + 3x^2 + 1\\) is divided by \\(x + 2\\), we can use the Remainder Theorem. The Remainder Theorem states that the remainder of the division of a polynomial \\(P(x)\\) by \\(x - c\\) is \\(P(c)\\). In this case, we are dividing by \\(x + 2\\), so we need to find \\(P(-2)\\).\n\nLet's break it down step by step:\n\n1. Substitute \\(x = -2\\) into each term of the polynomial.\n2. Simplify each term.\n3. Sum the simplified terms to get the remainder.\n\nLet's do this using Python code to ensure accuracy.\n```python\n# Define the polynomial function P(x)\ndef P(x):\n    term1 = (5 * x + 9) ** 611\n    term2 = (x + 5) ** 11\n    term3 = (x - 1) ** 11\n    term4 = 3 * x ** 2\n    term5 = 1\n    return term1 + term2 + term3 + term4 + term5\n\n# Substitute x = -2 into the polynomial\nremainder = P(-2)\nprint(remainder)\n```\n```output\n529\n```\nThe remainder when \\( (5x + 9)^{611} + (x + 5)^{11} + (x - 1)^{11} + 3x^2 + 1 \\) is divided by \\( x + 2 \\) is \\(\\boxed{529}\\).", "To find the remainder when the polynomial $(5x + 9)^{611} + (x + 5)^{11} + (x - 1)^{11} + 3x^2 + 1$ is divided by $x + 2$, we can use the Remainder Theorem. The Remainder Theorem states that the remainder of the division of a polynomial $f(x)$ by a linear divisor $x - c$ is $f(c)$. In this case, we need to find the value of the polynomial when $x = -2$.\n\nLet's break down the polynomial and evaluate it at $x = -2$:\n\n1. Evaluate $(5x + 9)^{611}$ at $x = -2$:\n   \\[\n   (5(-2) + 9)^{611} = (-10 + 9)^{611} = (-1)^{611} = -1.\n   \\]\n\n2. Evaluate $(x + 5)^{11}$ at $x = -2$:\n   \\[\n   (-2 + 5)^{11} = 3^{11}.\n   \\]\n\n3. Evaluate $(x - 1)^{11}$ at $x = -2$:\n   \\[\n   (-2 - 1)^{11} = (-3)^{11} = -