d_chemistry = 75\nstudents_calculus_and_physics = 30\n\n# Number of students taking at least one subject\nstudents_at_least_one_subject = total_students - students_no_subject\n\n# Using the principle of inclusion and exclusion\n# students_at_least_one_subject = students_calculus + students_physics + students_chemistry - students_calculus_and_physics - students_calculus_and_chemistry - students_physics_and_chemistry + students_all_three\n# Substituting students_chemistry = 2 * students_physics\n# students_at_least_one_subject = students_calculus + students_physics + 2 * students_physics - students_calculus_and_physics - students_calculus_and_chemistry - students_physics_and_chemistry + students_all_three\n# students_at_least_one_subject = students_calculus + 3 * students_physics - students_calculus_and_physics - students_calculus_and_chemistry - students_physics_and_chemistry + students_all_three\n# 345 = 180 + 3 * students_physics - 30 - 75 - 75 + 15\n# 345 = 180 + 3 * students_physics - 150 + 15\n# 345 = 45 + 3 * students_physics\n# 300 = 3 * students_physics\n# students_physics = 100\n\n# Let's solve for students_physics\nstudents_physics = (students_at_least_one_subject - students_calculus + students_calculus_and_physics + students_calculus_and_chemistry + students_physics_and_chemistry - students_all_three) // 3\nprint(students_physics)\n```\n```output\nNameError: name 'students_physics' is not defined\n```\nIt seems there is still an issue with the variable reference. Let's simplify the calculation and directly solve for the number of students taking physics using the derived equation.\n\nWe know:\n\\[ 345 = 180 + 3P - 30 - 75 - 75 + 15 \\]\n\\[ 345 = 45 + 3P \\]\n\\[ 300 = 3P \\]\n\\[ P = 100 \\]\n\nSo, the number of students taking physics is \\(100\\). Let's print this result directly.\n```python\n# Given values\ntotal_students = 360\nstudents_no_subject = 15\nstudents_all_three = 15\nstudents_calculus = 180\nstudents_chemistry = 2 * 100  # Since we solved f