n\n# Find the roots of the polynomial equation\nroots = sp.solve(polynomial, z)\n\n# Extract the roots\nroots = [sp.simplify(root) for root in roots]\n\n# Convert the roots to complex numbers\nroots = [complex(root.evalf()) for root in roots]\n\n# Calculate the area of the polygon formed by the roots\ndef polygon_area(vertices):\n    n = len(vertices)\n    area = 0\n    for i in range(n):\n        x1, y1 = vertices[i].real, vertices[i].imag\n        x2, y2 = vertices[(i + 1) % n].real, vertices[(i + 1) % n].imag\n        area += x1 * y2 - x2 * y1\n    return abs(area) / 2\n\narea = polygon_area(roots)\n\n# Simplify the area to the form p^(a/b)\narea_simplified = sp.nsimplify(area)\n\n# Extract p, a, and b from the simplified area\np = area_simplified.as_base_exp()[0]\na = area_simplified.as_base_exp()[1].as_numer_denom()[0]\nb = area_simplified.as_base_exp()[1].as_numer_denom()[1]\n\n# Calculate a + b + p\nresult = a + b + p\n\nprint(result)\n```\n```output\n2.0\n```\nIt seems there was an issue with the code execution. Let's break down the problem again and ensure we correctly find the roots of the polynomial and calculate the area of the polygon formed by these roots.\n\n1. **Find the roots of the polynomial equation \\(z^4 + 4z^3i - 6z^2 - 4zi - i = 0\\).**\n2. **Determine the vertices of the polygon in the complex plane.**\n3. **Calculate the area of the polygon.**\n4. **Express the area in the form \\(p^{a/b}\\) and find \\(a + b + p\\).**\n\nLet's use a different approach to find the roots and calculate the area. We'll use the `numpy` library to find the roots of the polynomial and then calculate the area of the polygon formed by these roots.\n\n```python\nimport numpy as np\n\n# Define the coefficients of the polynomial z^4 + 4z^3i - 6z^2 - 4zi - i = 0\ncoefficients = [1, 4j, -6, -4j, -1j]\n\n# Find the roots of the polynomial\nroots = np.roots(coefficients)\n\n# Extract the roots\nroots = [complex(root) for root in roots]\n\n# Calculate the area of the polyg