 minus the area of the larger sector plus the area of the triangle formed by the radii and the chord.\n\n5. **Set Up the Equation:**\n   - The total shaded area is the area of the larger circle minus the area of the smaller circle plus the overlapping area.\n   - The overlapping area is the area of the sector of the smaller circle minus the area of the sector of the larger circle plus the area of the triangle.\n   - The area of the triangle is \\(\\frac{1}{2} \\cdot 1 \\cdot 1 \\cdot \\sin(\\theta) = \\frac{\\sin(\\theta)}{2}\\).\n\n6. **Solve for \\(\\theta\\):**\n   - The equation becomes \\(\\frac{5\\pi}{3} = 4\\pi - \\pi + \\frac{\\theta \\pi}{360} - \\frac{\\theta \\pi}{90} + \\frac{\\sin(\\theta)}{2}\\).\n   - Simplifying, we get \\(\\frac{5\\pi}{3} = 3\\pi + \\frac{\\theta \\pi}{360} - \\frac{4\\theta \\pi}{360} + \\frac{\\sin(\\theta)}{2}\\).\n   - This simplifies to \\(\\frac{5\\pi}{3} = 3\\pi - \\frac{3\\theta \\pi}{360} + \\frac{\\sin(\\theta)}{2}\\).\n   - Further simplifying, we get \\(\\frac{5\\pi}{3} = 3\\pi - \\frac{\\theta \\pi}{120} + \\frac{\\sin(\\theta)}{2}\\).\n   - Rearranging terms, we get \\(\\frac{5\\pi}{3} - 3\\pi = -\\frac{\\theta \\pi}{120} + \\frac{\\sin(\\theta)}{2}\\).\n   - This simplifies to \\(-\\frac{4\\pi}{3} = -\\frac{\\theta \\pi}{120} + \\frac{\\sin(\\theta)}{2}\\).\n   - Multiplying through by 120, we get \\(-160\\pi = -\\theta \\pi + 60\\sin(\\theta)\\).\n   - Rearranging, we get \\(\\theta \\pi = 60\\sin(\\theta) + 160\\pi\\).\n   - Dividing by \\(\\pi\\), we get \\(\\theta = 60\\frac{\\sin(\\theta)}{\\pi} + 160\\).\n\nLet's use Python and sympy to solve this equation.\n\n```python\nimport sympy as sp\n\n# Define the variable\ntheta = sp.symbols('theta')\n\n# Define the equation\nequation = sp.Eq(theta, 60 * sp.sin(theta) / sp.pi + 160)\n\n# Solve the equation\nsolution = sp.solve(equation, theta)\nprint(solution)\n```\n```output\nNo algorithms are implemented to solve equation theta - 60*sin(theta)/pi - 160\n```\nIt seems 