roduct of $\\mathbf{a}$ and $\\mathbf{b}$ is given by:\n\\[\n\\mathbf{a} \\cdot \\mathbf{b} = |\\mathbf{a}| |\\mathbf{b}| \\cos(29^\\circ)\n\\]\n\nThe dot product of $\\mathbf{b}$ and $\\mathbf{a} - \\mathbf{b}$ is given by:\n\\[\n\\mathbf{b} \\cdot (\\mathbf{a} - \\mathbf{b}) = \\mathbf{b} \\cdot \\mathbf{a} - \\mathbf{b} \\cdot \\mathbf{b} = |\\mathbf{a}| |\\mathbf{b}| \\cos(29^\\circ) - |\\mathbf{b}|^2\n\\]\n\nSince the angle between $\\mathbf{b}$ and $\\mathbf{a} - \\mathbf{b}$ is $84^\\circ$, we can write:\n\\[\n\\mathbf{b} \\cdot (\\mathbf{a} - \\mathbf{b}) = |\\mathbf{b}| |\\mathbf{a} - \\mathbf{b}| \\cos(84^\\circ)\n\\]\n\nWe can also express the dot product $\\mathbf{a} \\cdot (\\mathbf{a} - \\mathbf{b})$ as:\n\\[\n\\mathbf{a} \\cdot (\\mathbf{a} - \\mathbf{b}) = \\mathbf{a} \\cdot \\mathbf{a} - \\mathbf{a} \\cdot \\mathbf{b} = |\\mathbf{a}|^2 - |\\mathbf{a}| |\\mathbf{b}| \\cos(29^\\circ)\n\\]\n\nSince the angle between $\\mathbf{a}$ and $\\mathbf{a} - \\mathbf{b}$ is $\\theta$, we can write:\n\\[\n\\mathbf{a} \\cdot (\\mathbf{a} - \\mathbf{b}) = |\\mathbf{a}| |\\mathbf{a} - \\mathbf{b}| \\cos(\\theta)\n\\]\n\nBy equating the two expressions for $\\mathbf{a} \\cdot (\\mathbf{a} - \\mathbf{b})$, we get:\n\\[\n|\\mathbf{a}|^2 - |\\mathbf{a}| |\\mathbf{b}| \\cos(29^\\circ) = |\\mathbf{a}| |\\mathbf{a} - \\mathbf{b}| \\cos(\\theta)\n\\]\n\nTo find $\\cos(\\theta)$, we need to express $|\\mathbf{a} - \\mathbf{b}|$ in terms of $|\\mathbf{a}|$ and $|\\mathbf{b}|$. Using the dot product expression for $\\mathbf{b} \\cdot (\\mathbf{a} - \\mathbf{b})$, we can solve for $|\\mathbf{a} - \\mathbf{b}|$:\n\\[\n|\\mathbf{b}| |\\mathbf{a} - \\mathbf{b}| \\cos(84^\\circ) = |\\mathbf{a}| |\\mathbf{b}| \\cos(29^\\circ) - |\\mathbf{b}|^2\n\\]\n\\[\n|\\mathbf{a} - \\mathbf{b}| \\cos(84^\\circ) = |\\mathbf{a}| \\cos(29^\\circ) - |\\mathbf{b}|\n\\]\n\\[\n|\\mathbf{a} - \\mathbf{b}| = \\frac{|\\mathbf{a}| \\cos(29^\\circ) - |\\mathbf{b}|}{\\cos(84^\\circ)}\n\\]\n\nNow we can subst