n# Dot product of a and a - b\na_dot_a_minus_b = a_norm**2 - a_dot_b\n\n# Equation for the angle between a and a - b\ncos_theta_a_a_minus_b_expr = a_dot_a_minus_b / (a_norm * a_minus_b_norm)\n\n# Substitute the values\ncos_theta_a_a_minus_b_value = cos_theta_a_a_minus_b_expr.subs({a_dot_b: a_norm * b_norm * sp.cos(sp.rad(theta_ab)), \n                                                                b_norm: sp.sqrt(a_norm**2 + b_norm**2 - 2 * a_norm * b_norm * sp.cos(sp.rad(theta_ab)))})\n\n# Simplify the expression\ncos_theta_a_a_minus_b_value = sp.simplify(cos_theta_a_a_minus_b_value)\n\n# Find the angle\ntheta_a_a_minus_b = sp.acos(cos_theta_a_a_minus_b_value)\ntheta_a_a_minus_b_deg = sp.deg(theta_a_a_minus_b)\n\nprint(theta_a_a_minus_b_deg)\n```\n```output\n180*acos((a_norm - b_norm*cos(pi/15))*sqrt(a_norm**2 - 2*a_norm*b_norm*cos(pi/15) + b_norm**2)/(a_norm*sqrt(a_norm**2 - 2*a_norm*b_norm*cos(pi/15) + b_norm**2)))/pi\n```\nIt looks like the output is a bit complicated, but we can simplify it further. Let's break it down step by step and simplify the expression manually.\n\nGiven:\n\\[\n\\cos \\theta_{a(a-b)} = \\frac{\\mathbf{a} \\cdot (\\mathbf{a} - \\mathbf{b})}{\\|\\mathbf{a}\\| \\|\\mathbf{a} - \\mathbf{b}\\|}\n\\]\n\nWe have:\n\\[\n\\mathbf{a} \\cdot (\\mathbf{a} - \\mathbf{b}) = \\|\\mathbf{a}\\|^2 - \\|\\mathbf{a}\\| \\|\\mathbf{b}\\| \\cos 29^\\circ\n\\]\nand\n\\[\n\\|\\mathbf{a} - \\mathbf{b}\\| = \\sqrt{\\|\\mathbf{a}\\|^2 + \\|\\mathbf{b}\\|^2 - 2 \\|\\mathbf{a}\\| \\|\\mathbf{b}\\| \\cos 29^\\circ}\n\\]\n\nSo,\n\\[\n\\cos \\theta_{a(a-b)} = \\frac{\\|\\mathbf{a}\\|^2 - \\|\\mathbf{a}\\| \\|\\mathbf{b}\\| \\cos 29^\\circ}{\\|\\mathbf{a}\\| \\sqrt{\\|\\mathbf{a}\\|^2 + \\|\\mathbf{b}\\|^2 - 2 \\|\\mathbf{a}\\| \\|\\mathbf{b}\\| \\cos 29^\\circ}}\n\\]\n\nSimplifying further:\n\\[\n\\cos \\theta_{a(a-b)} = \\frac{\\|\\mathbf{a}\\| - \\|\\mathbf{b}\\| \\cos 29^\\circ}{\\sqrt{\\|\\mathbf{a}\\|^2 + \\|\\mathbf{b}\\|^2 - 2 \\|\\mathbf{a}\\| \\|\\mathbf{b}\\|