e accuracy.\n```python\nimport math\n\n# Define the functions t and g\ndef t(x):\n    return 3 - g(x)\n\ndef g(x):\n    return math.sqrt(x)\n\n# Evaluate t(g(16))\nresult = t(g(16))\nprint(result)\n```\n```output\n1.0\n```\nThe final answer is \\( \\boxed{1} \\).", "To find the value of \\( t(g(16)) \\), we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. Compute \\( g(16) \\) using the function \\( g(x) = \\sqrt{x} \\).\n2. Substitute the result from step 1 into the function \\( t(x) = 3 - g(x) \\) to find \\( t(g(16)) \\).\n\nLet's break it down and solve it step-by-step using Python code.\n\n1. Compute \\( g(16) \\):\n\\[ g(16) = \\sqrt{16} = 4 \\]\n\n2. Substitute \\( g(16) \\) into \\( t(x) \\):\n\\[ t(g(16)) = t(4) = 3 - g(4) = 3 - \\sqrt{4} = 3 - 2 = 1 \\]\n\nNow let's verify this with Python code.\n```python\nimport math\n\n# Define the functions g(x) and t(x)\ndef g(x):\n    return math.sqrt(x)\n\ndef t(x):\n    return 3 - g(x)\n\n# Compute g(16)\ng_16 = g(16)\n\n# Compute t(g(16))\nt_g_16 = t(g_16)\nprint(t_g_16)\n```\n```output\n1.0\n```\nThe value of \\( t(g(16)) \\) is \\(\\boxed{1}\\).", "To find \\( t(g(16)) \\), we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. First, evaluate \\( g(16) \\).\n2. Then, substitute the result from step 1 into the function \\( t(x) \\).\n\nGiven:\n\\[ g(x) = \\sqrt{x} \\]\n\\[ t(x) = 3 - g(x) \\]\n\nLet's start by evaluating \\( g(16) \\):\n\\[ g(16) = \\sqrt{16} = 4 \\]\n\nNow, we substitute \\( g(16) = 4 \\) into \\( t(x) \\):\n\\[ t(g(16)) = t(4) = 3 - g(4) \\]\n\nSince \\( g(4) = \\sqrt{4} = 2 \\), we have:\n\\[ t(4) = 3 - 2 = 1 \\]\n\nSo, the final answer is:\n\\[ t(g(16)) = 1 \\]\n\nLet's confirm this with Python code.\n```python\nimport math\n\n# Define the functions g(x) and t(x)\ndef g(x):\n    return math.sqrt(x)\n\ndef t(x):\n    return 3 - g(x)\n\n# Calculate t(g(16))\nresult = t(g(16))\nprint(result)\n```\n```output\n1.0\n```\nThe calculated value of \\( t(g(16)) \\) is \\( 1 \\).\n\nSo, the final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{1}\n\\]", "To