ible perimeter of the triangle, given that two sides are each 8 units long and the third side has a whole number length, is \\(\\boxed{31}\\).", "To find the area of the trapezoid, we can use the formula for the area of a trapezoid:\n\n\\[ \\text{Area} = \\frac{1}{2} \\times (\\text{Base}_1 + \\text{Base}_2) \\times \\text{Height} \\]\n\nIn this trapezoid:\n- The lengths of the parallel sides (bases) are 5 cm and 9 cm.\n- The height of the trapezoid is 5 cm.\n\nLet's plug these values into the formula:\n\n\\[ \\text{Area} = \\frac{1}{2} \\times (5 + 9) \\times 5 = \\frac{1}{2} \\times 14 \\times 5 = 35 \\text{ square centimeters} \\]\n\nNow, let's confirm this with Python code.\n```python\n# Define the bases and height of the trapezoid\nbase1 = 5\nbase2 = 9\nheight = 5\n\n# Calculate the area of the trapezoid\narea = 0.5 * (base1 + base2) * height\nprint(area)\n```\n```output\n35.0\n```\nThe area of the trapezoid is \\(\\boxed{35}\\) square centimeters.", "To find the area of the trapezoid, we can use the formula for the area of a trapezoid:\n\n\\[ \\text{Area} = \\frac{1}{2} \\times (b_1 + b_2) \\times h \\]\n\nwhere \\( b_1 \\) and \\( b_2 \\) are the lengths of the two parallel sides (bases) and \\( h \\) is the height of the trapezoid.\n\nFrom the diagram, we can see that:\n- The lengths of the two parallel sides (bases) are 9 cm and 5 cm.\n- The height of the trapezoid is 5 cm.\n\nNow we can substitute these values into the formula:\n\n\\[ \\text{Area} = \\frac{1}{2} \\times (9 + 5) \\times 5 \\]\n\nLet's calculate this using Python to ensure accuracy.\n```python\n# Define the lengths of the bases and the height\nb1 = 9  # length of the first base in cm\nb2 = 5  # length of the second base in cm\nh = 5   # height of the trapezoid in cm\n\n# Calculate the area of the trapezoid\narea = 0.5 * (b1 + b2) * h\nprint(area)\n```\n```output\n35.0\n```\nThe area of the trapezoid is \\( \\boxed{35} \\) square centimeters.", "To find the area of the trapezoid, we can use the formula for the area of a trapezoid:\n\n\\[ \\text{Area} = \\frac{1}{2} \\times (\\text{Base}_1 + \\text{Base}_2) \\times \\text{Height} \\]\n\nIn this trapezoid, the bases are 5 cm and 9 cm, and the height is 5 cm. Let's substitute these values into the formula:\n\n\\[ \\text{Area} = \\frac{1}{2} \\times (5 + 9) \\times 5 \\]\n\nWe can calculate this step by step. First, we add the bases:\n\n\\[ 5 + 9 = 14 \\]\n\nThen we multiply by the height and divide by 2:\n\n\\[ \\text{Area} = \\frac{1}{2} \\times 14 \\times 5 = 7 \\times 5 = 35 \\]\n\nSo the area of the trapezoid is \\(35\\) square centimeters. Let's confirm this with Python code.\n```python\n# Define the bases and height of the trapezoid\nbase1 = 5\nbase2 = 9\nheight = 5\n\n# Calculate the area of the trapezoid\narea = 0.5 * (base1 + base2) * height\nprint(area)\n```\n```output\n35.0\n```\nThe area of the trapezoid is \\(\\boxed{35}\\) square centimeters.", "To find the area of the trapezoid, we can use the formula for the area of a trapezoid:\n\n\\[ \\text{Area} = \\frac{1}{2} \\times (b_1 + b_2) \\times h \\]\n\nwhere \\( b_1 \\) and \\( b_2 \\) are the lengths of the two parallel sides (bases), and \\( h \\) is the height of the trapezoid.\n\nFrom the diagram, we can see that the lengths of the two parallel sides are 5 cm and 9 cm, and the height is 5 cm. So, we can plug these values into the formula:\n\n\\[ \\text{Area} = \\frac{1}{2} \\times (5 + 9) \\times 5 \\]\n\nLet's calculate this step by step using Python to ensure accuracy.\n```python\n# Define the lengths of the bases and the height\nb1 = 5\nb2 = 9\nh = 5\n\n# Calculate the area of the trapezoid\narea = 0.5 * (b1 + b2) * h\nprint(area)\n```\n```output\n35.0\n```\nThe area of the trapezoid is \\(\\boxed{35}\\) square centimeters.", "To find the area of the trapezoid, we can use the formula for the area of a trapezoid:\n\n\\[ \\text{Area} = \\frac{1}{2} \\times (\\text{Base}_1 + \\text{Base}_2) \\times \\text{Height} \\]\n\nFrom the diagram, w