e))\n```", "To solve the problem, we need to determine the number of integers that satisfy the inequality \\(|x - 2| \\leq 5.6\\).\n\nFirst, let's break down the absolute value inequality:\n\n1. \\(|x - 2| \\leq 5.6\\)\n\nThis can be split into two inequalities:\n\n2. \\( -5.6 \\leq x - 2 \\leq 5.6 \\)\n\nNext, we solve these inequalities separately:\n\n3. \\( -5.6 \\leq x - 2 \\) and \\( x - 2 \\leq 5.6 \\)\n\nBy solving these, we get:\n\n4. \\( -5.6 + 2 \\leq x \\) and \\( x \\leq 5.6 + 2 \\)\n\n5. \\( -3.6 \\leq x \\leq 7.6 \\)\n\nNow, we need to find all integer solutions within the range \\([-3.6, 7.6]\\). The integers in this range are:\n\n-3, -2, -1, 0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7\n\nLet's count the number of integers in this range using Python code to ensure accuracy.\n```python\n# Define the range of possible integer solutions\nstart = int(-3.6)\nend = int(7.6)\n\n# Calculate the number of integers in the range\nnumber_of_integers = end - start + 1\nprint(number_of_integers)\n```\n```output\n11\n```\nThe number of integers in the solution set of \\(|x - 2| \\leq 5.6\\) is \\(\\boxed{11}\\).", "To solve the inequality \\(|x-2| \\leq 5.6\\), we need to understand what the absolute value inequality means. The inequality \\(|x-2| \\leq 5.6\\) can be rewritten as:\n\n\\[\n-5.6 \\leq x-2 \\leq 5.6\n\\]\n\nAdding 2 to all parts of the inequality, we get:\n\n\\[\n-5.6 + 2 \\leq x \\leq 5.6 + 2\n\\]\n\nThis simplifies to:\n\n\\[\n-3.6 \\leq x \\leq 7.6\n\\]\n\nNow, we need to find all the integers within this range. The integers from -3 to 7 inclusive are: -3, -2, -1, 0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, and 7. So, there are 11 integers in this range.\n\nLet's write the Python code to verify this.\n```python\n# Define the range based on the inequality -3.6 <= x <= 7.6\nstart = int(-3.6)  # This will be -3\nend = int(7.6)     # This will be 7\n\n# Generate the list of integers in the range and count them\ninteger_list = list(range(start, end + 1))\nnumber_of_integers = len(integer_list)\n\n