iven values\ntotal_boxes = 10\nboxes_with_pencils = 5\nboxes_with_pens = 4\nboxes_with_both = 2\n\n# Using the principle of inclusion and exclusion\nboxes_with_either_or_both = boxes_with_pencils + boxes_with_pens - boxes_with_both\n\n# Boxes with neither pens nor pencils\nboxes_with_neither = total_boxes - boxes_with_either_or_both\nprint(boxes_with_neither)\n```\n```output\n3\n```\nThe number of boxes that contain neither pens nor pencils is \\(\\boxed{3}\\).", "To determine how many boxes contain neither pens nor pencils, we can use the principle of inclusion and exclusion.\n\nHere's the breakdown of the problem:\n\n1. We have 10 boxes in total.\n2. 5 boxes contain pencils.\n3. 4 boxes contain pens.\n4. 2 boxes contain both pens and pencils.\n\nUsing the principle of inclusion and exclusion, the number of boxes that contain either pens or pencils (or both) is given by:\n\\[ \\text{Number of boxes with pens or pencils} = \\text{Number of boxes with pencils} + \\text{Number of boxes with pens} - \\text{Number of boxes with both} \\]\n\\[ = 5 + 4 - 2 = 7 \\]\n\nSo, 7 boxes contain either pens, pencils, or both. Therefore, the number of boxes that contain neither pens nor pencils is:\n\\[ \\text{Number of boxes with neither pens nor pencils} = \\text{Total number of boxes} - \\text{Number of boxes with pens or pencils} \\]\n\\[ = 10 - 7 = 3 \\]\n\nLet's confirm this with Python code.\n```python\n# Total number of boxes\ntotal_boxes = 10\n\n# Number of boxes with pencils\nboxes_with_pencils = 5\n\n# Number of boxes with pens\nboxes_with_pens = 4\n\n# Number of boxes with both pens and pencils\nboxes_with_both = 2\n\n# Using the principle of inclusion and exclusion to find the number of boxes with either pens or pencils or both\nboxes_with_either = boxes_with_pencils + boxes_with_pens - boxes_with_both\n\n# Number of boxes with neither pens nor pencils\nboxes_with_neither = total_boxes - boxes_with_either\nprint(boxes_with_neither)\n```\n```output\n3\n```\nThe number o