g in sign and the coefficients of \\( f(1) \\) are powers of 2. Let's express the general term \\( f(n) \\) in terms of \\( f(1) \\) and look for a pattern.\n\nBy examining the recurrence relation, we can hypothesize that:\n\\[ f(n) = a_n - b_n f(1) \\]\nwhere \\( a_n \\) and \\( b_n \\) are sequences that we need to determine.\n\nFrom the recurrence relation, we have:\n\\[ f(n + 1) = (-1)^{n + 1} n - 2f(n) = (-1)^{n + 1} n - 2(a_n - b_n f(1)) \\]\n\\[ f(n + 1) = (-1)^{n + 1} n - 2a_n + 2b_n f(1) \\]\n\nBy comparing with \\( f(n + 1) = a_{n + 1} - b_{n + 1} f(1) \\), we get:\n\\[ a_{n + 1} = (-1)^{n + 1} n - 2a_n \\]\n\\[ b_{n + 1} = 2b_n \\]\n\nThe sequence \\( b_n \\) is straightforward:\n\\[ b_1 = 1 \\]\n\\[ b_n = 2^{n - 1} \\]\n\nThe sequence \\( a_n \\) can be determined by solving the recurrence relation:\n\\[ a_1 = 0 \\]\n\\[ a_2 = 1 \\]\n\\[ a_3 = -4 \\]\n\\[ a_4 = 11 \\]\n\\[ a_5 = -26 \\]\n\nWe can observe that:\n\\[ a_n = (-1)^n (2^{n - 1} - 1) \\]\n\nSo, the general term is:\n\\[ f(n) = (-1)^n (2^{n - 1} - 1) - 2^{n - 1} f(1) \\]\n\nGiven \\( f(1) = f(1986) \\), we have:\n\\[ f(1) = (-1)^{1986} (2^{1985} - 1) - 2^{1985} f(1) \\]\n\\[ f(1) = 2^{1985} - 1 - 2^{1985} f(1) \\]\n\\[ f(1) + 2^{1985} f(1) = 2^{1985} - 1 \\]\n\\[ f(1) (1 + 2^{1985}) = 2^{1985} - 1 \\]\n\\[ f(1) = \\frac{2^{1985} - 1}{2^{1985} + 1} \\]\n\nNow, we need to find the sum \\( f(1) + f(2) + f(3) + \\dots + f(1985) \\):\n\\[ \\sum_{n=1}^{1985} f(n) = \\sum_{n=1}^{1985} \\left( (-1)^n (2^{n - 1} - 1) - 2^{n - 1} f(1) \\right) \\]\n\\[ = \\sum_{n=1}^{1985} (-1)^n (2^{n - 1} - 1) - \\sum_{n=1}^{1985} 2^{n - 1} f(1) \\]\n\nThe first sum is:\n\\[ \\sum_{n=1}^{1985} (-1)^n (2^{n - 1} - 1) = \\sum_{n=1}^{1985} (-1)^n 2^{n - 1} - \\sum_{n=1}^{1985} (-1)^n \\]\n\\[ = \\sum_{n=1}^{1985} (-1)^n 2^{n - 1} + 1 \\]\n\nThe second sum is:\n\\[ \\sum_{n=1}^{1985} 2^{n - 1} f(1) = f(1) \\sum_{n=1}^{1985} 2^{n - 1} = f(1) (2^{1985} - 1) \\]\n\nSo, the total sum is:\n\\[ \\sum_{n=1}^{1985} f(n) = \\sum_{n=