tance % 1\nfraction_numerator = fractional_part.as_integer_ratio()[0]\nfraction_denominator = fractional_part.as_integer_ratio()[1]\n\n# Simplify the fraction\nfrom math import gcd\ncommon_divisor = gcd(fraction_numerator, fraction_denominator)\nsimplified_fraction_numerator = fraction_numerator // common_divisor\nsimplified_fraction_denominator = fraction_denominator // common_divisor\n\n# Display the result as a mixed number\nmixed_number = f"{whole_part} {simplified_fraction_numerator}/{simplified_fraction_denominator}" if simplified_fraction_numerator != 0 else f"{whole_part}"\nprint(mixed_number)\n```\n```output\n137 1/2\n```\nThe car would travel \\(\\boxed{137 \\frac{1}{2}}\\) miles in \\(2 \\frac{3}{4}\\) hours.', "To determine how far a car travels at a speed of 50 miles per hour over a time of \\(2 \\frac{3}{4}\\) hours, we can use the formula for distance:\n\n\\[\n\\text{distance} = \\text{speed} \\times \\text{time}\n\\]\n\nFirst, we need to convert the mixed number \\(2 \\frac{3}{4}\\) to an improper fraction. \n\n\\[\n2 \\frac{3}{4} = 2 + \\frac{3}{4} = \\frac{8}{4} + \\frac{3}{4} = \\frac{11}{4}\n\\]\n\nNow, we can multiply the speed (50 miles per hour) by the time (\\(\\frac{11}{4}\\) hours):\n\n\\[\n\\text{distance} = 50 \\times \\frac{11}{4}\n\\]\n\nLet's perform this calculation step-by-step using Python to ensure accuracy.\n```python\n# Define the speed and time\nspeed = 50  # miles per hour\ntime = 11 / 4  # hours\n\n# Calculate the distance\ndistance = speed * time\nprint(distance)\n```\n```output\n137.5\n```\nThe distance calculated is 137.5 miles. To express this as a mixed number, we recognize that:\n\n\\[\n137.5 = 137 \\frac{1}{2}\n\\]\n\nThus, the car would travel \\( \\boxed{137 \\frac{1}{2}} \\) miles in \\(2 \\frac{3}{4}\\) hours at a speed of 50 miles per hour.", 'To find out how far a car would travel at a speed of 50 miles per hour for \\(2 \\frac{3}{4}\\) hours, we can use the formula for distance:\n\n\\[ \\text{Distance} = \\text{S