n the numerator and denominator cancel out:\n\\[\n\\frac{\\log{3}}{\\log{2}} \\cdot \\frac{\\log{4}}{\\log{3}} \\cdot \\frac{\\log{5}}{\\log{4}} \\cdot \\frac{\\log{6}}{\\log{5}} \\cdot \\frac{\\log{7}}{\\log{6}} \\cdot \\frac{\\log{8}}{\\log{7}} = \\frac{\\log{8}}{\\log{2}}.\n\\]\n\nSince \\(\\log{8} = \\log{2^3} = 3\\log{2}\\), we have:\n\\[\n\\frac{\\log{8}}{\\log{2}} = \\frac{3\\log{2}}{\\log{2}} = 3.\n\\]\n\nThus, the value of the expression is \\(3\\). Let's confirm this with Python code.\n```python\nimport math\n\n# Calculate the value of the expression using the change of base formula\nlog2_3 = math.log(3, 2)\nlog3_4 = math.log(4, 3)\nlog4_5 = math.log(5, 4)\nlog5_6 = math.log(6, 5)\nlog6_7 = math.log(7, 6)\nlog7_8 = math.log(8, 7)\n\nresult = log2_3 * log3_4 * log4_5 * log5_6 * log6_7 * log7_8\nprint(result)\n```\n```output\n3.0\n```\nThe value of the expression \\(\\log_2{3} \\cdot \\log_3{4} \\cdot \\log_4{5} \\cdot \\log_5{6} \\cdot \\log_6{7} \\cdot \\log_7{8}\\) is \\(\\boxed{3}\\).", "To find the value of \\(\\log_2{3} \\cdot \\log_3{4} \\cdot \\log_4{5} \\cdot \\log_5{6} \\cdot \\log_6{7} \\cdot \\log_7{8}\\), we can use the change of base formula for logarithms. The change of base formula states that \\(\\log_a{b} = \\frac{\\log_c{b}}{\\log_c{a}}\\) for any positive base \\(c\\). Using this formula, we can rewrite each term in the product as follows:\n\n\\[\n\\log_2{3} = \\frac{\\log{3}}{\\log{2}}, \\quad \\log_3{4} = \\frac{\\log{4}}{\\log{3}}, \\quad \\log_4{5} = \\frac{\\log{5}}{\\log{4}}, \\quad \\log_5{6} = \\frac{\\log{6}}{\\log{5}}, \\quad \\log_6{7} = \\frac{\\log{7}}{\\log{6}}, \\quad \\log_7{8} = \\frac{\\log{8}}{\\log{7}}\n\\]\n\nWhen we multiply these terms together, we get:\n\n\\[\n\\log_2{3} \\cdot \\log_3{4} \\cdot \\log_4{5} \\cdot \\log_5{6} \\cdot \\log_6{7} \\cdot \\log_7{8} = \\left(\\frac{\\log{3}}{\\log{2}}\\right) \\cdot \\left(\\frac{\\log{4}}{\\log{3}}\\right) \\cdot \\left(\\frac{\\log{5}}{\\log{4}}\\right) \\cdot \\left(\\