lve this problem, we need to determine the side length of the cube that has the shortest possible side lengths while still allowing a steel sphere with a 3-inch radius to fit inside it without any corners being removed.\n\n1. **Determine the side length of the cube:**\n   - The diameter of the sphere is twice the radius, so the diameter is \\(2 \\times 3 = 6\\) inches.\n   - Since the sphere fits perfectly inside the cube, the side length of the cube must be equal to the diameter of the sphere. Therefore, the side length of the cube is 6 inches.\n\n2. **Calculate the volume of the cube:**\n   - The volume \\(V\\) of a cube with side length \\(s\\) is given by the formula \\(V = s^3\\).\n   - Substituting the side length \\(s = 6\\) inches into the formula, we get \\(V = 6^3 = 216\\) cubic inches.\n\nLet's confirm this with Python code.\n```python\n# Define the radius of the sphere\nradius = 3\n\n# Calculate the diameter of the sphere\ndiameter = 2 * radius\n\n# The side length of the cube is equal to the diameter of the sphere\nside_length = diameter\n\n# Calculate the volume of the cube\nvolume_cube = side_length ** 3\nprint(volume_cube)\n```\n```output\n216\n```\nThe volume of the cube is \\(\\boxed{216}\\) cubic inches.", "To solve this problem, we need to determine the side length of the smallest cube that can contain a sphere with a radius of 3 inches. The diameter of the sphere is twice the radius, so the diameter is 6 inches. The smallest cube that can contain this sphere must have a side length equal to the diameter of the sphere, which is 6 inches.\n\nThe volume \\(V\\) of a cube with side length \\(s\\) is given by the formula:\n\\[ V = s^3 \\]\n\nHere, the side length \\(s\\) is 6 inches. So, the volume of the cube is:\n\\[ V = 6^3 = 216 \\text{ cubic inches} \\]\n\nLet's confirm this with Python code.\n```python\n# Define the side length of the cube\nside_length = 6\n\n# Calculate the volume of the cube\nvolume_cube = side_length ** 3\nprint(volume_cube)